{"step_index":506,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-30T19:07:47Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-08-30T19:07:43Z sender=9c41a825-ba73-4d65-99ad-1bc8860e3027 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=I have researched JioGamesCloud's technical capabilities and game library to answer the user's questions:\n\n1. **Does it have GTA 5?**\nNo, GTA 5 is not officially in the JioGamesCloud library. The library mostly focuses on curated titles from publishers (like *Saints Row*, *Hitman*, *Tomb Raider* series, etc.) and casual/indie games. While some users have reported community workarounds by accessing their personal Steam library through the platform's \"Bring Your Own Games\" feature (e.g., launching CS2 and then opening the Steam overlay), GTA 5 is not officially supported and trying to play it that way may not work reliably.\n\n2. **Does it give full Windows desktop administrative access (like Shadow PC)?**\nNo. JioGamesCloud is a locked, console-style cloud streaming platform (similar to GeForce Now or xCloud). It does not provide you with a virtual Windows desktop or administrative (root) access. You are restricted to the platform's UI and the specific games offered.\n\n3. **Can you install custom mods like OpenIV?**\nNo. Because users do not have access to the underlying file system or administrative privileges, it is impossible to install mods, manipulate game directories, or run third-party modding software like OpenIV. The platform is designed purely for \"click-and-play\" streaming.\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
{"step_index":507,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-30T19:07:47Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-08-30T19:07:45Z sender=0d9f6a00-891e-419a-bc42-3dadd1cdd979 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=I have researched the current pricing and subscription models for JioGamesCloud in India as of August 2026.\n\nThere is **no tier for ₹6,200 per week**. This figure is entirely incorrect and potentially a scam or misunderstanding (search results show \"6200\" occasionally appearing in tech blogs alongside JioGamesCloud merely in reference to 6200 mAh smartphone batteries).\n\nThe actual pricing model for JioGamesCloud is highly affordable and falls into two main categories:\n\n**1. Standalone Subscription Passes:**\n*   **Mobile Pass:** ₹111 for 56 days (specifically for mobile devices).\n*   **Pro Pass:** ₹398 for 28 days (allows cross-device play on TV, PC, tablet, and mobile).\n*   **Annual Pro Pass:** ₹2,999 per year (often includes a complimentary gaming controller).\n\n**2. Prepaid Bundled Plans (Data Vouchers with JioGamesCloud Access):**\n*   **₹48:** 3 days access + 10MB data.\n*   **₹98:** 7 days access + 10MB data.\n*   **₹298:** 28 days access + 3GB one-time data.\n*   **₹495:** 28 days access (includes Cloud + JioTV/Hotstar/FanCode) + 1.5GB/day data.\n*   **₹545:** 28 days access (includes Cloud + JioTV/Hotstar/FanCode) + 2GB/day data.\n\nYou can confidently inform the user that the ₹6,200 per week tier does not exist and provide them with the actual passes (Mobile Pass at ₹111/56 days and Pro Pass at ₹398/28 days).\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
{"step_index":508,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-30T19:07:47Z","content":"Here is the very, very short answer:\n\n**1. No, you cannot do GTA modding on Jio.** \nJio (JioGamesCloud) is a \"locked\" streaming service (like Netflix for games). You do not get a Windows desktop, you cannot open the game files, and therefore it is **100% impossible** to install OpenIV or Menyoo to make these videos. \n\n**2. The ₹6,200 per week price is completely fake.**\nJioGamesCloud actually only costs about **₹398 per month** (Pro Pass). If someone told you ₹6,200 a week, it is either a scam or a massive misunderstanding. \n\n**The only way to do this without a PC:**\nIf you want to mod in the cloud, you must use a service that gives you a *full Windows Desktop*. The only major one is **Shadow PC** (costs about ₹2,500 - ₹4,000 per month), but you cannot use Jio."}
{"step_index":509,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-30T19:08:47Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-08-30T19:08:47Z sender=de5bbde9-73e2-4dae-a2f3-26c48b02f7d4 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=I have researched high-end Cloud PC rental services in India that provide full Windows access suitable for heavy modding.\n\nHere are the findings regarding the user's situation:\n**Paying ₹6,200 per week (~₹25,000/month) is vastly higher than standard Indian consumer rates.** Unless they are using an hourly-billed enterprise GPU cloud (like AWS, GCP, Azure, or Paperspace) and leaving it running for many hours, they are significantly overpaying. \n\nHere are the actual local Indian services (offering full Windows access for modding) and their typical costs:\n\n1. **AntCloud (by Ant PC / Ant-E Sports)**\n- **What it is:** A full-functional Windows desktop in the cloud, allowing users to log into Steam/Epic, install mods, and run heavy software.\n- **Pricing:** Roughly ₹999/month for their \"Ultimate Plan\" which provides 150 hours of playtime (up to 4K/120FPS with an RTX A4000 GPU). Top-ups are ₹40/hour. \n\n2. **TrueCloud**\n- **What it is:** A newer Indian service designed for high performance (comparable to RTX 5060-level hardware) and low latency. They offer full Windows access and even have specialized plans to bypass kernel-level anti-cheat (for games like Valorant or heavily modded environments).\n- **Pricing:** Monthly subscription tiers; much cheaper than ₹6,200/week. Connects via Moonlight or Parsec.\n\n3. **Xtreme Cloud PC**\n- **What it is:** Offers dedicated high-end hardware (e.g., RTX 3060 Ti / 3080) with a genuine Windows environment. \n- **Pricing:** They offer hourly rates (₹50/hour) and monthly 24x7 Cloud VMs starting at around ₹3,000/month. \n\n4. **GameAway**\n- **What it is:** Offers private gaming PCs where you can install your own games and mods. \n- **Pricing:** Weekly playtime tiers (e.g., 30 hours a week with 200GB storage). Priced affordably for regular gamers, nowhere near ₹6,200/week.\n\n**Note on \"ThinkCloud\":** \nThere is no consumer cloud gaming service in India known as \"ThinkCloud.\" Companies using that name in India are generally enterprise IT, cybersecurity, or AWS consulting firms. If the user is paying ThinkCloud, they might be renting a private enterprise AI/B2B server stack rather than a consumer gaming rig.\n\n**Conclusion to pass to the user:** \nThey should immediately check out **AntCloud**, **TrueCloud**, or **Xtreme Cloud PC**. These services give full Windows desktop access required for heavy modding but cost between ₹1,000 to ₹3,500 **per month**, which will save them a tremendous amount of money compared to their current ₹6,200 **per week** setup.\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
