{"step_index":450,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-30T20:20:13Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-31T01:50:13+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-31T01:50:13+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/efc75235-355e-455c-b598-1a3e644f6697/bytesized_analysis.md`\nTotal Lines: 158\nTotal Bytes: 5771\nShowing lines 1 to 30\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # @bytesizedexplainer (Byte Sized Explainer) — Full NexLev Channel Analysis\n2: \n3: > **All data sourced from NexLev MCP — zero assumptions.**\n4: > **Date**: August 30, 2026\n5: \n6: ---\n7: \n8: ## 1. Channel Profile (NexLev Data)\n9: \n10: | Field | Value |\n11: |-------|-------|\n12: | **Channel Name** | Byte Sized Explainer |\n13: | **Handle** | @bytesizedexplainer |\n14: | **Channel ID** | `UCqUTa0HvxmUsmSrGJsmglPw` |\n15: | **Country** | United States |\n16: | **Joined** | May 4, 2023 (account old, but active content ~12 months) |\n17: | **Subscribers** | **183,000** |\n18: | **Total Views** | **19,357,170** (19.4M) |\n19: | **Videos** | **24** |\n20: | **Has Shorts** | No — Long-form only |\n21: | **Avg Video Duration** | ~8:38 (518 seconds) |\n22: | **Family Safe** | Yes |\n23: | **Has Contact Email** | No |\n24: | **Narration** | **Text-to-Speech (TTS)** — no human voice! |\n25: | **Description** | \"I use text-to-speech for narration because my place is too noisy to record clean audio\" |\n26: | **NexLev Category** | **Tech** |\n27: | **Content Style** | Tech explainer — OS comparisons, CPU breakdowns, screen resolutions |\n28: \n29: > [!NOTE]\n30: > **Uses TTS narration** — this creator doesn't even record their own voice. Proof that you don't need a mic, studio, or voice skills to make \\$8K/month on YouTube.\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":451,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-30T20:20:13Z","content":"Now I have everything I need. Let me create the skill:","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"YouTube Channel Audit skill for automated channel analysis using NexLev MCP","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"---\nname: youtube-channel-audit\ndescription: >\n  Automated YouTube channel audit and analysis using NexLev MCP tools.\n  Extracts channel profile, RPM, revenue, demographics, monetization status,\n  lifetime earnings, and per-video efficiency metrics. Outputs a structured\n  markdown report artifact. MUST activate whenever the user says \"analyze this\n  channel\", \"audit this channel\", \"channel analysis\", \"check this channel\",\n  \"how much is this channel earning\", \"do the same analysis\", \"do it for this\n  channel\", provides a YouTube channel screenshot, mentions a YouTube handle\n  (@username), or wants to know a channel's RPM, revenue, demographics, or\n  monetization status. Also activate when the user pastes a YouTube channel URL\n  or provides a channel name and wants financial/audience data.\n---\n\n# YouTube Channel Audit\n\nRun a complete NexLev-powered channel audit for any YouTube channel and output a structured markdown report artifact.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- User provides a channel handle (@username), screenshot, or URL\n- User says \"analyze\", \"audit\", \"check\", \"do the same\", \"for this channel too\"\n- User asks about RPM, revenue, earnings, demographics, monetization\n- User wants to compare channels\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- NexLev MCP must be authenticated (tokens at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.mcp-auth\\`)\n- NexLev caller scripts at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\`\n- NEVER rewrite the NexLev scripts — just call them\n\n## Audit Workflow\n\nExecute these steps in order. Each step uses NexLev MCP via the Python caller scripts.\n\n### Step 1: Get Channel Handle\n\nExtract the YouTube handle from:\n- Screenshot (read @handle from the image)\n- URL (extract from youtube.com/@handle)\n- User message (they'll say the handle or channel name)\n\n### Step 2: Fetch Channel Profile\n\nCall `youtube_channel_about` with the handle:\n\n```\nSet-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_audit.json\" -Value '{\"username\": \"HANDLE_HERE\"}' -Encoding UTF8\npython \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_call.py\" youtube_channel_about \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_audit.json\"\n```\n\nExtract these fields from the response:\n- `channelId` — needed for all subsequent calls\n- `title` — channel name\n- `channelHandle` — @handle\n- `subscriberCount` — subscriber count\n- `viewCount` — total lifetime views\n- `videosCount` — total videos\n- `country` — creator country\n- `joinedDate` — channel creation date\n- `description` — channel description\n- `isFamilySafe` — family safe status\n- `hasEmail` — business email availability\n- `tabs` — check for \"Shorts\" tab to determine if channel has Shorts\n- `links` — social media links\n- `keywords` — channel keywords\n\n### Step 3: Fetch RPM, Revenue & Demographics\n\nCall `get_geography_revenue` with the channel ID:\n\n```\nSet-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_rpm.json\" -Value '{\"channelId\": \"CHANNEL_ID_HERE\"}' -Encoding UTF8\npython \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_call.py\" get_geography_revenue \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_rpm.json\"\n```\n\nExtract these fields:\n- `channelType` — LONG_ONLY, SHORT_ONLY, or MIXED\n- `revenue.month_revenue` — estimated monthly revenue\n- `revenue.month_long_revenue` — monthly long-form revenue\n- `revenue.month_short_revenue` — monthly Shorts revenue\n- `revenue.long_view_count` — monthly long-form views\n- `revenue.short_view_count` — monthly Shorts views\n- `revenue.channel_category_rpm` — category average RPM\n- `revenue.channel_long_rpm` — channel's long-form RPM\n- `revenue.channel_short_rpm` — channel's Shorts RPM\n- `revenue.weighted_avg_duration` — average video duration in seconds\n- `revenue.channel_language_code` — content language\n- `demographics.gender` — male/female/user_specified percentages\n- `demographics.age` — age group distribution (13-17, 18-24, 25-34, 35-44, 45-54, 55-64, 65+)\n- `demographics.viewership_country` — top 5 countries by view share\n- `category` — NexLev content category\n\n### Step 4: Monetization Check (Optional — on request)\n\nCall `check_channel_monetization` with the channel ID:\n\n```\nSet-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_mon.json\" -Value '{\"channelId\": \"CHANNEL_ID_HERE\"}' -Encoding UTF8\npython \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_call.py\" check_channel_monetization \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_mon.json\"\n```\n\n### Step 5: Calculate Derived Metrics\n\nFrom the raw NexLev data, calculate:\n\n| Metric | Formula |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Lifetime Earnings** | `total_views × channel_long_rpm / 1000` |\n| **Channel Age** | `today - joinedDate` (in months) |\n| **Average Monthly Earning** | `lifetime_earnings / channel_age_months` |\n| **Revenue per Video** | `lifetime_earnings / total_videos` |\n| **Views per Video** | `total_views / total_videos` |\n| **Subs per Video** | `subscribers / total_videos` |\n| **Tier 1 Traffic %** | Sum of US + UK + Canada + Australia percentages |\n\n### Step 6: Generate Report Artifact\n\nCreate a markdown artifact at: `{channel_handle}_analysis.md`\n\n## Report Template\n\nUse this EXACT structure for every report:\n\n```markdown\n# @{handle} ({channel_name}) — Full NexLev Channel Analysis\n\n> **All data sourced from NexLev MCP — zero assumptions.**\n> **Date**: {current_date}\n\n---\n\n## 1. Channel Profile (NexLev Data)\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Channel Name** | {name} |\n| **Handle** | @{handle} |\n| **Channel ID** | `{id}` |\n| **Country** | {country} |\n| **Joined** | {joined_date} (**~{age_months} months ago**) |\n| **Subscribers** | {subs} |\n| **Total Views** | **{views}** |\n| **Videos** | {video_count} |\n| **Has Shorts** | {yes/no based on tabs} |\n| **Avg Video Duration** | ~{duration_formatted} |\n| **Family Safe** | {yes/no} |\n| **Has Contact Email** | {yes/no} |\n| **Description** | \"{description_excerpt}\" |\n| **NexLev Category** | **{category}** |\n| **Content Style** | {brief content description from videos/description} |\n\n---\n\n## 2. RPM & Revenue (NexLev — Real Data)\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Category RPM** | **${category_rpm}** |\n| **Channel Long-form RPM** | **${long_rpm}** |\n| **Estimated Monthly Revenue** | **${month_revenue}** |\n| **Monthly Long-form Revenue** | ${long_revenue} |\n| **Monthly Long-form Views** | {long_views} |\n| **Channel Type** | {channel_type} |\n| **Weighted Avg Duration** | {duration} |\n| **Channel Language** | {language} |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Total Lifetime Earnings Estimate\n\n| Calculation | Value |\n|------------|-------|\n| Total views | {total_views} |\n| Channel RPM | ${long_rpm} |\n| **Estimated total lifetime earnings** | **~${lifetime_earnings}** |\n| Months active | ~{months} |\n| **Average monthly earning** | **~${avg_monthly}/month** |\n| **Current monthly earning** | **${current_monthly}/month** |\n| **Revenue per video** | **${rev_per_video}** |\n| **Views per video** | **{views_per_video}** |\n\n> [!NOTE/IMPORTANT/TIP]\n> Add a contextual insight about the channel's growth trajectory\n> (growing, declining, or stable) by comparing current monthly vs lifetime average.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Audience Demographics (NexLev — Real Data)\n\n### Gender Split\n| Gender | % |\n|--------|---|\n| **Male** | **{male}%** |\n| Female | {female}% |\n\n### Age Distribution\n| Age Group | % |\n|-----------|---|\n| 13-17 | {pct}% |\n| 18-24 | {pct}% |\n| 25-34 | {pct}% |\n| 35-44 | {pct}% |\n| 45-54 | {pct}% |\n| 55-64 | {pct}% |\n| 65+ | {pct}% |\n\n### Geographic Distribution\n| Country | % of Views |\n|---------|-----------|\n| {country_1} | {pct}% |\n| {country_2} | {pct}% |\n| {country_3} | {pct}% |\n| {country_4} | {pct}% |\n| {country_5} | {pct}% |\n\n> Add insight about Tier 1 traffic percentage and how it affects RPM.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Key Videos (From Screenshot or NexLev)\n\n| Title | Views | Age | Length |\n|-------|-------|-----|--------|\n| {video_1} | {views} | {age} | {length} |\n| {video_2} | {views} | {age} | {length} |\n| {video_3} | {views} | {age} | {length} |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Comparison (if other channels have been analyzed in this session)\n\nAdd a comparison table with ALL previously analyzed channels if available.\n\n---\n\n## Dat